      "title": "Investors at COP31 warn of rising systemic financial risk",
      "content_html": "Forty large pension funds, insurers and sovereign wealth funds warned at the COP31 climate summit in Antalya that climate impacts threaten financial stability. Investors at a closed-door meeting said climate finance needs private capital, but some asset owners remain cautious about emerging-market projects because they lack reliable ways to assess and manage the risks.\n\nDeveloping countries including India are pressing for clearer obligations and more adaptation funding, while the European Union favors using existing finance mechanisms rather than creating a new work program. Outside the talks, organizers said more than 10,000 people joined a Nov. 14 climate march calling for grants, support for affected communities and a transition away from fossil fuels. Negotiators have a 104-paragraph climate-finance draft, released Nov. 14, and are due to continue discussions on finance and a just transition in the summit’s second week.",
