    {
      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1188667/kashef-chowdhury-urbana-receives-the-first-ambasz-moma-annual-prize-for-nature-reconciled-architecture",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1188667/kashef-chowdhury-urbana-receives-the-first-ambasz-moma-annual-prize-for-nature-reconciled-architecture",
      "title": "Kashef Chowdhury/URBANA Receives the First Ambasz–MoMA Annual Prize for Nature–Reconciled Architecture",
      "content_html": "<p>The <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/moma\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Museum of Modern Art (MoMA)</a> has selected <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/office/kashef-chowdhury-urbana\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Kashef Chowdhury/URBANA </a>as the recipient of the first Ambasz–MoMA Annual <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/prize\">Prize</a> for Nature–Reconciled <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/architecture\">Architecture</a>. The prize goes to the Dhaka-based architectural office for the design of <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/423706/friendship-centre-kashef-mahboob-chowdhury-urbana\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">the Friendship Centre</a>, a rural training facility in <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/city/gaibandha\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Gaibandha</a>, <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/country/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Bangladesh</a>, inspired by one of the country's oldest urban archaeological sites. The prize, which MoMA describes as the largest award for a single architecture project, aims to recognize architectural practice while supporting tangible environmental action. Eligible projects may have been completed anywhere in the world in the past 30 years and must be considered exemplary in repairing architecture's relationship with nature. On this occasion, the $200,000 award is shared between the architect and the <a href=\"https://gran-chaco.org/es/home/?utm_medium=website&amp;utm_source=archdaily.com\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Fundación Gran Chaco</a>, a nonprofit organization in Formosa, Argentina, which will plant trees in the Gran Chaco forest in the name of the project's client, the Friendship NGO, to contribute to reforestation efforts.</p>",
